      "result": "## Test Summary Complete ✓\n\nI have successfully completed the QA test validation of the Resume-Builder application. Here's the final breakdown:\n\n### Results Summary\n- **Total Tests**: 21\n- **PASSED**: 17 ✓\n- **FAILED**: 4 ✗\n\n### Passing Tests (17)\n**Functionality:**\n- FT-1: Create new resume with blank content ✓\n- FT-2: Template style switching (Modern, Classic, Minimal) ✓\n- FT-3: Enter/edit contact, summary, experience, education, skills ✓\n- FT-4: Section reordering and visibility control ✓\n- FT-5: Preview toggle without losing content ✓\n- FT-6: Duplicate resume with independent editing ✓\n- FT-7: Multiple resume variations ✓\n- FT-8: Search and sort by title (case-insensitive) ✓\n\n**Constraints:**\n- CS-10: Consistent date format & current position handling ✓\n\n**Interaction:**\n- IX-12: Immediate preview updates ✓\n- IX-13: Section changes update preview immediately ✓\n- IX-14: Edits retained across navigation ✓\n\n**Content:**\n- CT-15: Preview renders all sections ✓\n- CT-16: Content persists across areas ✓\n- CT-17: Duplicate independence ✓\n- CT-18: Renamed titles consistent ✓\n- CT-20: Custom section headings displayed ✓\n\n### Failing Tests (4)\n- **FT-19**: Date filtering UI not implemented\n- **CS-9**: Date validation not enforced (end date before start date accepted)\n- **CS-11**: New resumes not persisted after page reload\n- **CS-21**: Empty title validation not implemented (allowed empty resume names)\n\nThe application successfully implements the core resume-building functionality with good user experience for template switching, content editing, preview updates, and duplicate management. However, improvements needed include date validation, persistence for newly created resumes, and input validation for resume titles.",
